<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - December 12.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - December 12.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading</p>
<p>and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand,</p>
<p>Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Dec 12    Dec 5</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 325-350  325-350</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok	615	 615</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB  235	 235</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)  250-290   250-290</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port    273-280     280</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port     265-270     270</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50</p>
<p>U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     19.50-20.00 19.50-20.00</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
</text>
